<!--Post: 11026--><!--Time: 1110369732-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11026"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:topsailgrl@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 4:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/11087344.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/11087344.htm</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>Ammendment 1: <BR> <BR> <BR>Congress shall make no law respecting an establishment of religion, or prohibiting the free exercise thereof; or abridging the freedom of speech, or of the press; or the right of the people peaceably to assemble, and to petition the government for a redress of grievances.  <BR> <BR>Where do these city officials get off? I understand that they want to keep the case in Sedwick County but jeez, threatening people? A little over stepping here if you ask me. I think the voters in Sedwick county need to take a good hard long look at the ballots next time around.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11026-->
<!--Post: 11032--><!--Time: 1110382451-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11032"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Witchking<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Witchking<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 7:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->After this case and the LIES about family members not wanting to be contacted when in fact it was Wichita PD TELLING Them not to talk, to Sedgewick County employees being &#39;warned&#39; to keep quiet and in general the 30 plus years of chasing their tails with no clear strategy over how this killer was to be caught or the media used &#40;like telling them if the doll were made public it might incite him again---hogwash, HE SENT IT, he laid it in a public park&#41; I&#39;d clean house. New Sheriff, new prosecutor, new EVERYTHING, a fresh start if you will. Don&#39;t keep anyone from previous. To move forward Wichita and Sedgewick County need fresh faces and new approaches. No holdover warhorses. <BR> <BR>Wichita PD wanted the media on their side for years and now they give them and everyone else the back of their hands including the citizens of your fair city &#40;which I found to be homespun and warm&#41;. <BR> <BR>Hey, Park City has already strated the housecleaning by getting rid of their no good compliance officer---other cities should follow suit or the voters should do it for them. They NEED to be held accountable for 30 years not just credited with one...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11032-->
<!--Post: 11039--><!--Time: 1110386244-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11039"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 8:37 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Classic case of &#34;what a tangled web we weave when first we practice to deceive&#34;. They have cover-ups about cover-ups about cover-ups to the point that they are so desperate now, they&#39;re trying to declare martial law and rescind the constitution to cover their asses. <BR> <BR>I would be nice being on the money end of any lawsuit that arises from a city or county employee being fired for discussing the case &#40;who hasn&#39;t signed a contract or taken an oath that would make them bound by the order&#41;. The only problem is that something like this could bankrupt Wichita.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11039-->
<!--Post: 11050--><!--Time: 1110391181-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11050"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:topsailgrl@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 9:59 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I hear ya! They would have to subpoena every county or city employee to place a judge ordered gag order to make this legal! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11050-->
<!--Post: 11058--><!--Time: 1110398180-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11058"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 11:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I don&#39;t believe THAT was a good idea, makes people like us dig more t find out what they are hiding.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11058-->
<!--Post: 11604--><!--Time: 1110934519-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11604"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brown_tornado<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brown_tornado<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 4:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->there are several people in our city&#39;s leadership that need to be replaced. That fat ass Nola Foulston &#40;D.A.&#41; would be my first choice to kick her ass outta here.  <BR>So many times we&#39;ve asked for information, but NOOOOOOOOOO, the P.D. are just too good to give ANYTHING out. You now see where it got them, 31 YEARS LATER. AND, they still wouldn&#39;t have caught BTK if he didn&#39;t make the mistake he did.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11604-->
<!--Post: 11664--><!--Time: 1111016799-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11664"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 3:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->INteresting point to be made today. Scott Peterson was given the death penalty. Good call, but Rader is not, any one want to talk about that, It is not LE&#39;s fault, it is the fault of the government, and whos rights they are protecting<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11664-->
<!--Post: 11674--><!--Time: 1111019659-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11674"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 4:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->WKing, <BR> <BR>If this is all true and I don&#39;t doubt your word then it points to one thing: who was protecting Rader ? <BR> <BR>Is it possible that Rader had a close friend in politics or LE who protected him, knowing he was BTK, from investigation through out the case ? <BR> <BR>I understand the gag order being a way to make sure that info is not leaked that would lead to a huge civil suit cash case against the city BUT is there more to it ? <BR> <BR>30&#43; years ago it was speculated that the Zodiac had a LE official protecting him from investigation. Nothing was ever proven.  .  .   <BR> <BR>The shocked reaction of the church leader made me think that maybe Rader had friends willing to help him no matter what the cost.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11674-->
<!--Post: 11718--><!--Time: 1111045078-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11718"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 16, 2005 - 11:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->As far as Rader not getting the death penalty...now here is a switch, California has a death penalty, but Kansas doesn&#39;t...didn&#39;t, do now. Actually thought we did but the wording wasn&#39;t quite right, so it was declared unconstituional. <BR> <BR>Apparently the part that was supposed to say &#34;...convicted of capital murder will be put to death by means of lethal injection...&#34; actually read &#34;...convicted of the slaying of a free man or woman or slave of a free man or woman shalt be executed in the public square by hanging by the neck till dead...or something to that effect. <BR> <BR>However, what is the worst punishment: painless death, or life in prison &#40;death by boredom&#41;. The original idea behind capital punishment was to get them to hell before they had time to repent. However, how can we be absolutely sure there is a hell? <BR> <BR>I think it would be wise to hedge our bets. When someone is convicted of a capital crime they should get life in prison but also: For each meal they would be required to file a request for food, explaining in detail why they are in prison and need the food. This would apply to every meal that they eat for the rest of their lives. They would get one half hour of TV which would be a rerun of the nightly news from five years earlier, that has been shortened to add extra medicine commercials. If they flushed their toilet more than once a day it would back up. Their morning coffee would be decaffinated. They would have to work eight hours a day typing miscellaneous archives to the state web page using a sticky keyboard for 1 cent per 25 correct words, and the proceeds used to pay their legal fees and victim compensation. they would also have to pay for their meals, medical, dental, electric bill, and water bill. Their exercise would be a treadmill in a closet &#40;charge for gym fee&#41;. there would also be a special charge to keep the truck horn on their wall from blowing every 30 minutes at night. Any time they fell behind on their other bills the money from the truck horn fee would be applied to the other accounts.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11718-->
